==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{q|idiomatic}} {{l|en|shut up like a clam}}

===Etymology===
By analogy with a {{m|en|clam}} closing itself.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-clam up.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|slang}} To become [[silent]]; to [[stop]] [[talking]], to [[shut up]].
#* '''1986''', {{w|Paul Chadwick}}, ''Concrete: Under the Desert Stars'', Dark Horse Books
#*: Maybe he … or she … was a witness who refused to '''clam up''' … a whistle blower …
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To make or become [[clammy]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|shut up}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|talk}}

